# Copy to .env (git-ignored). `docker compose` reads it automatically.

# JWT signing secret. REQUIRED: compose and the backend refuse to start without
# it. Startup also rejects obviously unsafe values (under 32 characters, a known
# placeholder, a repeated pattern), but passing those checks does not make a
# value random. Always generate it with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Changing it later signs every user out (existing tokens become invalid).
SECRET=

# First administrator: when BOTH are set and no superuser exists, the server
# creates this as a NEW account on startup. Use an email that has no account yet;
# an existing account is never promoted. Password: at least 12 characters.
# Remove FIRST_ADMIN_PASSWORD from this file after the first successful start.
FIRST_ADMIN_EMAIL=
FIRST_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# hCaptcha (optional)
# HCAPTCHA_ENABLED=true
# HCAPTCHA_SECRET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HCAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
